          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E L_\infty
              \-algebras
            is meant to be the fully
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theoretic
            (i.e.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,0)
              \-
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorified
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+structure"} higher structure
            enhancing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} mathematical structure
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
            %em and
            the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exterior+algebra"} skew symmetry
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
            are relaxed up to potentially infinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+law"} coherent
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+homotopy"} higher homotopy
          %p
            This is in contrast to the more widely considered notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebras"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
            but retain strict
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exterior+algebra"} skew symmetry
            = succeed "\u201D:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E L_\infty
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
